\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Finite fields and operator products}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{A field assigns a coefficient to each vertex or edge. Endpoint
pullbacks compare values on these distinct spaces. Composition then
supplies an operator product on a common field module, and its relation
to pointwise multiplication returns us to a discrete product rule.
The [four-cycle](fdip-0003) recovers coordinates and exhibits the
resulting noncommutativity.}
\p{The coefficient ring is commutative and unital; the operator product
need not commute. Positive counting pairings and weights enter only in
the [real specialization](fdip-0002). The product-first viewpoint has a
geometric-algebra precedent in
\citet{author-PDF pp. 5-6, Equations (1.1)-(1.6)}{hestenes1986unified};
Doran and Lasenby explain their delayed use of coordinates in
\citet{Preface, p. x}{doran2003geometric}. Here the product is composition
of specified maps, not an assumed Clifford geometric product.}

